## 2. Autonomic Reflex Stratum Partition (tau <= 100 microseconds)

The openOODA architecture enforces the Reflexive Encapsulation Law (RFC 0020 Section 5):
  is_autonomic_reflex_stratum(G) = true  <=>  1 <= G <= 4

Operations in Generations 1 through 4 execute in an immutable, deterministic, zero-heap substrate:
1. Deterministic Execution Bound:
   For all G in {1, 2, 3, 4}: tau_exec(G) <= tau_max(G) <= 100 microseconds.
2. Zero Ambient I/O Blocking:
   Autonomic reflexes never block on mutex locks, network sockets, or filesystem descriptors.
3. Bump Arena Memory Model:
   Allocations use O(1) bump pointers in pre-allocated linear memory arenas (chs_rt_arena.c).
   Arena bulk resets eliminate garbage collection pauses and memory allocation drag (D_alloc -> 0).

## 3. Formal State Transition Tensor

Let S_k^(G) represent the full internal state of generation tier G at discrete cycle k.
Inter-generational state evolution follows the state transition tensor T:
  S_(k+1)^(G) = T_(G, G') * S_k^(G') + Phi_G(Obs_k, Dec_k)

Where:
- T_(G, G') defines coupling coefficients between generation tiers.
- Lower tiers (Gen 1-3) pass filtered sensor states and kinematic tracking upwards.
- Higher tiers (Gen 5-7) project policy weights, strategic constraints, and objective functions downward.
- Reflex bypass operators provide immediate short-circuit control without waiting for higher-tier convergence.

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                           INTER-GENERATIONAL TENSOR PROJECTION MATRIX                           │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Tier Matrix Form:                                                                               │
│   [ S_(k+1)^(Gen 7) ]   [ T_77  T_76  0     0     0     0     0    ] [ S_k^(Gen 7) ]   [ Psi_7 ]│
│   [ S_(k+1)^(Gen 6) ]   [ T_67  T_66  T_65  0     0     0     0    ] [ S_k^(Gen 6) ]   [ Psi_6 ]│
│   [ S_(k+1)^(Gen 5) ]   [ 0     T_56  T_55  T_54  0     0     0    ] [ S_k^(Gen 5) ]   [ Psi_5 ]│
│   [ S_(k+1)^(Gen 4) ] = [ 0     0     T_45  T_44  T_43  0     0    ] [ S_k^(Gen 4) ] + [ Psi_4 ]│
│   [ S_(k+1)^(Gen 3) ]   [ 0     0     0     T_34  T_33  T_32  0    ] [ S_k^(Gen 3) ]   [ Psi_3 ]│
│   [ S_(k+1)^(Gen 2) ]   [ 0     0     0     0     T_23  T_22  T_21 ] [ S_k^(Gen 2) ]   [ Psi_2 ]│
│   [ S_(k+1)^(Gen 1) ]   [ 0     0     0     0     0     T_12  T_11 ] [ S_k^(Gen 1) ]   [ Psi_1 ]│
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## 4. Implicit Guidance & Control (IG&C) and Feedback Mechanics

The OODA architecture contains four primary feedback channels:

1. Action -> Observe (Sensory Feedback):
   Physical actuation alters the environment. New sensor readings reflect kinetic changes.
2. Action -> Orient (Kinetic Confirmation):
   Actuator state sensors confirm mechanical execution directly to internal models.
3. Orient -> Observe (Attention Gating):
   Orientation models direct sensor gaze, adjust radar beam steering, and set filter thresholds.
4. Orient -> Act (Autonomic Reflex Bypass / IG&C):
   When immediate survival threats occur, Orientation triggers actuation directly.
   The reflex bypass circumvents the high-latency Decide phase (tau <= 100 microseconds).

## 5. Demarcation of Gen 7 Swarm Kinematics

The standard library modules gen7_swarm.oo and singularity_cannon.oo implement 2D particle kinetics
and distributed multi-node coordination algorithms.
In this architectural audit, these modules are formally demarcated as:
- Synthetic phenomenological benchmarks for multi-agent swarm coordination.
- They evaluate relative position error (delta_p <= 2.5 px) and inter-agent communication.
- They do not represent full General Relativity Einstein field equations or Quantum Field Theory solutions.
- True relativistic physics modules reside in std/phys/astrodynamics/ and std/phys/quantum/.
